  "question": {
    "text": "A thin spherical conducting shell of radius $\\mathrm{R}$ has a charge $\\mathrm{q}$. Another charge $\\mathrm{Q}$ is placed at the centre of the shell. The electrostatic potential at a point $\\mathrm{P}$ a distance $\\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{2}$ from the centre of the shell is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZdCqD",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 R}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tCMJb",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 \\mathrm{Q}}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{R}}-\\frac{2 \\mathrm{q}}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{R}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UyY7K",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2 Q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 R}+\\frac{q}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 R}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "w3yy9",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{(\\mathrm{q}+\\mathrm{Q}) 2}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{R}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Potential due to spherical shell, $\\mathrm{v}_1=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{R}}$. Potential difference due to charge at the centre\n$\\mathrm{V}_2=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{Q}}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 r} ; \\mathrm{V}=\\mathrm{V}_1+\\mathrm{V}_2=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{Q}}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{R}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{R}}$",
    "image": null
